{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: panel is pure cross-sectional mean reversion at all horizons (raw ret SR -0.9 to -1.05 at 3/20/60/120/250; vol, skew, kurt, beta, corrm all dead; vol-conditioning via mul destroys it). Combining a short leg ret(20) with a long leg ret(250), optionally vol-scaled, plus optional ret(3)/minr(250) legs, forms a dense cluster of 10+ variants at SR 1.40-1.53 with IC ~0.010; construction (cs_rank vs cs_z), weights, and leg swaps barely move it, and delay(3) retains ~87 pct of SR, indicating slow decay and robustness to the 1-day lag. Stopping at 6 of 12 batches (~118 exprs) to limit selection bias. Reporting: the leader (20 + vol-scaled 250), a 4-leg ensemble (3, 20, scaled 250, minr 250) expected to shrink least OOS, and the parsimonious core pair (20 + 250) as a low-fit anchor.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:31:16.569766+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["neg(add(cs_rank(ret(20)), cs_rank(div(ret(250), std(250)))))", "neg(add(add(cs_rank(ret(3)), cs_rank(ret(20))), add(cs_rank(div(ret(250), std(250))), cs_rank(minr(250)))))", "neg(add(cs_rank(ret(20)), cs_rank(ret(250))))"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.5318, 1.504, 1.4517], "rationale": "Panel exhibits robust cross-sectional mean reversion at every horizon while all other feature families (vol, skew, kurt, beta, corrm) are dead. All three picks are multi-horizon reversal blends from a dense cluster of 10+ construction variants scoring SR 1.40-1.53 in train with IC ~0.010: (1) rank-blend of 20d reversal with vol-scaled 250d reversal (train SR 1.53); (2) a 4-leg rank ensemble adding ret(3) and minr(250) legs (SR 1.50) expected to shrink least out of sample; (3) the parsimonious core pair of 20d and 250d reversal (SR 1.45) as a minimal-fitting anchor. Family robustness: parameter neighbors consistent, z vs rank construction consistent, and delay(3) retains ~87 pct of SR, indicating slow signal decay.", "n_batches_used": 6, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:31:23.644303+00:00"}
